## Summary of Changes

### 1. Headless Dedicated Server Mode (`--headless`)
* **Modified File:** `src/com/hartrusion/rbmksim/RbmkSimulator.java`
* **Description:** Added support for the `--headless` command-line argument in `main(String[] args)`. When launched with `--headless`, the application skips Swing/AWT look-and-feel and window initialization and immediately starts the TCP `SocketServer` on port `26486` alongside the 100 ms cyclic simulation loop.

### 2. UDP Multiplayer Player Position Relay
* **Added File:** `src/com/hartrusion/rbmksim/UdpPlayerRelay.java`
* **Modified Files:** `src/com/hartrusion/rbmksim/RbmkSimulator.java`, `src/com/hartrusion/rbmksim/MainLoop.java`
* **Description:** Added a lightweight `DatagramSocket` relay thread listening on UDP port `26486` (started automatically in `--headless` mode and via the `StartServer` action). Tracks active player endpoints and broadcasts 3D player position/rotation packets between connected clients, pruning inactive clients after 5 seconds.

### 3. Thread-Safe State Loading & Null-Property Guard
* **Modified File:** `src/com/hartrusion/rbmksim/MainLoop.java`
* **Description:** Added a synchronization lock (`simLock`) around `run()`, `SaveSimulationState`, and `LoadSimulationState` so `.ic` save files are never serialized or deserialized mid-cycle while the simulation thread is executing. Wrapped the registered `ModelListener` controller in a null-filtering proxy (`safeController`) in `init()` to prevent `NullPointerException` crashes in `ConcurrentHashMap` when deserialized components emit null property updates after switching save files, and guarded `ExceptionPopup.show()` in headless environments.

### 4. Build & Packaging Automation
* **Added File:** `build.ps1`
* **Description:** Added a PowerShell build pipeline using `javac`, `jar`, and `jpackage` to compile the Java sources, bundle dependencies and embedded mnemonic display resources into `RbmkSimulator.jar`, generate a portable Windows runtime image (`RbmkServer.exe`), and collect all required GPL-3.0, MIT, and OpenJDK license notices into a `Legal/` directory.
